-- chem/inertiasound.cub — the sign that the inertia engine (chem/inertia.cub) counts, and the first steps of its
-- elimination, proved. Jacobi's rule reads the number of negative eigenvalues of N as the number of negative pivots of
-- N = LDLᵀ, the k-th pivot being D_k/D_{k−1}, a quotient of consecutive leading minors, whose sign is the sign of the
-- product D_{k−1}·D_k. The engine counts a sign change at step k when bit-eq (bz-pos D_{k−1}) (bz-pos D_k) is false.
-- Proved here: (i) for nonzero binary integers in canonical form, when that test is true the product is positive and
-- when it is false the product is negative, so every change counted is a negative pivot and every step not counted a
-- positive one (`in-pivot-sign`); (ii) each division the elimination makes is exact whenever its remainder is zero,
-- (n/d)·d = n for either sign of n (`in-exact`), and division by 1 always is (`in-div-one`); (iii) so the first step,
-- whose previous pivot is 1, yields the 2×2 minors a·e − c·b exactly, and the engine's second minor is the leading
-- 2×2 minor of its input (`in-second-minor`). Not proved here: that every later division's remainder is zero
-- (Sylvester's identity: the k-th step's entries are (k+1)×(k+1) minors, divisible by the previous pivot), hence that
-- every minor the engine returns is a leading principal minor; and the assembly of the congruence N = LDLᵀ over lists.
import "inertia.cub"

import "h2ground.cub"
